      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Overview",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Use the Background Assets API to manage content that Apple hosts, so people can download that content outside your main app bundle on the App Store. You submit asset packs to app review; your app can have:",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "To learn more about integrating Apple-hosted background assets into your app, see `https://developer.apple.com/documentation/backgroundassets/downloading-asset-packs-hosted-by-apple` and to learn more about validating the behavior of your background assets, see `https://developer.apple.com/documentation/backgroundassets/testing-asset-packs-locally`.",
          "refs": [
            "https://developer.apple.com/documentation/backgroundassets/downloading-asset-packs-hosted-by-apple",
            "https://developer.apple.com/documentation/backgroundassets/testing-asset-packs-locally"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "To manage Apple-hosted background assets, be sure you have one of the following user roles:",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": [
        {
          "text": "Multiple background asset packs",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Versions of asset packs, each with unique content",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "One active beta version and one App Store version per asset pack",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Updates to content without creating a new app version",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "`ADMIN`",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "`APP MANAGER`",
          "refs": []
        },
